      "writtenOn": "2023-09-15T15:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Comment added.\n\nSkReadBuffer first looks at the SkImage `dProcs.fImageProc` and if it is non-null, tries to use it. If the result or the proc was null, it then falls back to all the registered codecs. I think that addresses your concerns in general that a user does not *need* to call `SkCodecs::Register` if they properly set the SkSerialProcs and SkDeserialProcs.",
      "parentUuid": "545a16ac_33f2465e",
